diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..45ffeef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Posting as a bot
+
+In Account settings, choose **Set up chat bots**, add a bot, then copy its bot code. Bots start with no room memberships. Add a bot using a room's membership settings, or turn on **Add to all open rooms** to join every current and future open room. Turning it off keeps existing memberships.
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --data-binary 'Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅' \
+  "https://chat.example.com/rooms/${ROOM_ID}/${BOT_CODE}/messages"
+```
+
+Send UTF-8 text, not a JSON object. Use `--data-binary @filename` to keep newlines when reading a file. Success returns `201` with the message location. A blank body returns `422`, an invalid credential returns `401`, and a missing or inaccessible room returns `404`.
+
+Treat the code as a password: use HTTPS, store it in your CI secret store, and keep the full URL out of shell traces and proxy access logs. Campfire removes the code from the path before Rails logs requests; upstream servers need their own redaction. Delete the bot to revoke the code. Existing messages retain their author.
+
+## Responding to webhook events
+
+Set **Webhook URL** on the bot to receive a JSON POST when a room member selects it from the @-mention menu. Use a publicly reachable HTTPS endpoint; Campfire blocks private network destinations and does not follow redirects. Clear the field to stop callbacks.
+
+The first time a bot with a webhook is added to a room, Campfire sends a `joined` event with just `event` and `room` (id, name and `reply_to`). Direct conversations do not send this event.
+
+The `mention` event includes `author` (id and name), `room` (id, name and `reply_to`), and `message` (id, `body.text`, `body.html` and `link`). Use the text for the command, without the bot's own mention, or the HTML for the complete message. Both paths are relative to your Campfire origin. The `reply_to` path contains the bot code: keep it out of logs.
+
+Return `200` with UTF-8 `text/plain` or `text/html` to post a reply immediately. To defer a reply, return `204`, then POST plain text to `room.reply_to` as above. Deliveries run in the background; replies larger than 1 MiB are ignored.
+
+## Cooldowns and suspension
+
+A bot can post ten messages in a rolling ten-second window across all its rooms. API posts and webhook replies share this limit. The next post is rejected and starts a 30-second cooldown. Wait for the number of seconds in the API’s `Retry-After` header before retrying a `429`. Webhook replies during cooldown are dropped, not deferred. Five further posting attempts during the same cooldown suspend the bot.
+
+Ten consecutive failed webhook deliveries also suspend a bot. A non-`2xx` response, timeout, or connection error counts as a failure; any `2xx` response resets the streak, even if it contains no reply.
+
+Suspended bots receive no webhooks, and their posting endpoint returns `403`. Their memberships, messages, and place in the owner's bot limit are unchanged. The bots page shows the reason for suspension. An administrator can choose **Reactivate** there to clear the suspension and reset the counters.
diff --git a/lib/middleware/bot_request.rb b/lib/middleware/bot_request.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82ac450
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/middleware/bot_request.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Extract the credential before request logging and keep Rack's form parser
+# (including method override) from interpreting a shell script's raw text.
+class BotRequest
+  PATH = %r{\A(/rooms/[^/]+/)([^/]+)(/messages/?)\z}
+
+  def initialize(app)
+    @app = app
+  end
+
+  def call(env)
+    if match = PATH.match(env["PATH_INFO"])
+      env["campfire.bot_code"] = match[2]
+      env["PATH_INFO"] = "#{match[1]}filtered#{match[3]}"
+      env["REQUEST_URI"] = env["REQUEST_URI"].sub(match[0], env["PATH_INFO"]) if env["REQUEST_URI"]
+      env["CONTENT_TYPE"] = "text/plain" if env["REQUEST_METHOD"] == "POST"
+    end
+    @app.call(env)
+  end
+end
